---
description: Enforce practical SEO baseline for public pages
alwaysApply: true
---

# SEO first

- Every public page must define metadata via `buildPageMetadata` (or `generateMetadata`) — title + description.
- Titles must be meaningful and not generic.
- Descriptions must be human-readable and not placeholders on shipped pages.
- Ensure one H1 per page; maintain heading hierarchy; use semantic HTML.
- Pages must be indexable unless explicitly `noIndex`.
- Canonicals via `buildPageMetadata` / `getSiteUrl` — home uses trailing `/`.
- JSON-LD: `{pageName}PageSchema()` on the page; shared helpers only in `lib/schema.ts` (see `json-ld-page-schema.mdc`).
- Keep internal links on `paths.ts` / nav / footer config.
